body:
`SettingsViewModelTest > the invitations switch is on by default, loads from prefs and leaves the collaborator switch alone (T-319)` fails under the parallel gate with `kotlinx.coroutines.test.UncompletedCoroutinesError at TestBuilders.kt:353`, and `InboxSeenInvitesTest` (T-322) has timed out the same way in the same kind of run. Both pass alone and in other full runs.

Evidence, all on 2026-10-31 on a 12-core / 31 GB host running `./verify-all.sh` in parallel mode (Gradle, vitest and pytest workers at once):
- the T-368 subagent's first Android stage: both tests timed out; both green when run alone and in its next full run;
- the orchestrator's gate on the guests integration branch (`/tmp/verify-all.JNQSbs/android-test-lint.log`): `SettingsViewModelTest` failed, 763 tests, 1 failed; the class alone passed straight after; the guests change (T-366/T-367/T-368) touches nothing on `SettingsViewModel`'s path;
- the baseline gate on `main` at cde16cb1 passed.

Probably the same shape as T-358 (web `OverviewPage` flake under load): a `runTest` whose collector or child coroutine is still pending when the body returns under scheduler starvation. Look at how the test waits for the prefs flow, and whether `advanceUntilIdle`/`closeWhenIdle` is missing before the assertion, rather than raising the timeout.
